WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
Xian fills this grid with numbers.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.560
He places the numbers from one to five

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.660
in the five squares in the bottom row,
in some order.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.400
In the next two rows,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.420
each square contains the sum of the numbers

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.760
in the three closest squares in the row below.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.500
The arrows indicate how this addition works

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.580
for the first square in the second row.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.780
What is the largest possible value

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.340
of the number in the top square?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.760
This is a maximising problem.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.840
We will count how often
each bottom number contributes.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.080
The centre counts three times,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.250
its neighbours twice, and the ends once.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.720
Put five centrally,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.300
three and four beside it,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.910
and one and two at the ends.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.040
Larger numbers in more-counted positions
give a larger total.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.060
The middle sums are nine, twelve, eleven.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.840
The maximum is thirty-two: answer C.
